From 58dabd7f8f45b3dc9a7addaf7c9c1c94ced6a228 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 15:45:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign AI vehicle inspection engine: component-by-component
 findings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the old per-shot pass/fail verdict (which produced generic
'matches baseline' / 'no changes' text) with a component-by-component
report: every named part (bumper, headlights, seats, dashboard trim,
etc.) visible in a shot gets its own Verified / Unable to Verify / New
Finding verdict with a factual description and confidence score,
instead of guessing at low-confidence areas.

Server-side (analyze-inspection edge function, deployed):
- New per-component Gemini prompt per shot, scoped to the specific
  parts expected in that angle (SHOT_COMPONENTS)
- Never guesses: low-confidence/obstructed/blurry components come back
  as 'unable_to_verify' with a retake recommendation instead of a
  fabricated verdict
- New aggregate report shape: shots[], newFindings[], unableToVerify[],
  areasInspected/areasVerified counts, real summary bullets and
  recommendation generated from actual findings

Client-side:
- New ShotInspectionCard component renders each shot as a scannable
  card: overall match %, then Verified / Unable to Verify / New
  Findings sections — replaces the old single-line PhotoComparisonRow
- Owner's Vehicle Health Report screen rewired to the new report shape,
  with top-level New Findings and Unable to Verify summary sections
  above the full component-by-component breakdown
